1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,438
Sworn is for Tempo Zones: private ledgers where only the operator sees every transaction.

2
00:00:06,488 --> 00:00:10,145
Before a Zone business releases a withdrawal batch,

3
00:00:10,195 --> 00:00:15,706
a counterparty may need to check it; without evidence, settlement may wait.

4
00:00:15,756 --> 00:00:18,950
Sworn creates verifiable evidence without exposing transactions.

5
00:00:19,000 --> 00:00:25,382
The operator selects the batch in Sworn's local console and starts a proof job.

6
00:00:25,432 --> 00:00:30,436
Sworn runs Tempo's own Zone verification code in a zero-knowledge VM,

7
00:00:30,486 --> 00:00:35,950
then creates proof evidence that a third party can verify on chain.

8
00:00:36,000 --> 00:00:40,558
On Moderato, our own one-operator Zone, not a Tempo-created one,

9
00:00:40,608 --> 00:00:47,470
settles a batch only after Sworn's proof passes; only then can a withdrawal be paid.

10
00:00:47,520 --> 00:00:50,695
Three batches, proven and checked on chain.

11
00:00:50,745 --> 00:00:55,764
A forged batch, even signed by our own sequencer, is rejected.

12
00:00:55,814 --> 00:00:59,450
Anchor to payout: fifty-eight minutes, on one laptop.

13
00:00:59,500 --> 00:01:05,011
First buyer: a Zone business whose reviewer cannot reconstruct the private witness.

14
00:01:05,061 --> 00:01:09,645
A signed report or generic proof may not be enough:

15
00:01:09,695 --> 00:01:13,816
the reviewer may need evidence of exact Tempo execution.

16
00:01:13,866 --> 00:01:18,450
One batch tests demand; repeats or upgrades become Proof Operations.

17
00:01:18,500 --> 00:01:23,080
Sworn is Tempo-specific, not generic ZK: it runs Zone code,

18
00:01:23,130 --> 00:01:26,783
fits the portal's batch shape, and tracks upgrades.

19
00:01:26,833 --> 00:01:30,950
We begin as Proof Operations for a Zone business.

20
00:01:31,000 --> 00:01:37,894
Later, Tempo could add this as an independent check alongside its TEE, not replace it.

21
00:01:37,944 --> 00:01:43,450
I work on Reth and Revm, with fifteen years in banking systems.

22
00:01:43,500 --> 00:01:45,783
Today: testnet, unaudited, market unproven.

23
00:01:45,833 --> 00:01:47,183
No customer claimed.

24
00:01:47,233 --> 00:01:54,650
Next, a design partner supplies a batch and decides if independent proof is worth paying for.

25
00:01:54,700 --> 00:01:57,450
Sworn: audit-ready evidence for private execution.
